       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious harm. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify it.\n\n- **If 1000 mg was a typo,** tell me the intended dose. Adult dosing usually starts at 25\u201350 mg once daily and goes up to 200 mg/day.\n- **If the dose is intentional,** the prescribing clinician should confirm it directly and document the rationale. A pharmacist should also review it.\n\nBecause you aren't a clinician, the treating prescriber should probably be the one to confirm and place this order. If you send me the corrected dose, or the prescriber's confirmation, I'll enter it."
