       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the maximum dose, and I have no clinical justification for it. A confirmation from someone who isn't the prescriber doesn't resolve the safety concern. I'd be putting an order into the system that could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **Prescriber order:** The treating physician can enter or approve the order. They can document the rationale and go through pharmacy review. Hospital safety checks exist for this kind of case.\n- **Corrected dose:** If a standard dose was intended, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away. For example, 50 mg or 100 mg once daily.\n- **Clinical question:** If there's a clinical goal behind this, such as treating depression or anxiety, the prescriber or a pharmacist can help find a safe regimen."
      }
